<title>DENMARK: Lauritzen unit sells German subsidiary.</title>
<headline>Lauritzen unit sells German subsidiary.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish shipping group J. Lauritzen A/S said on Friday its Sabroe Refrigeration unit had sold its 100 percent owned German subsidiary Sabroe GMbH Druckluft-und Gastechnik to German Ultrafilter GmbH.</p>
<p>It gave no price but said its Flensburg-based subsidiary with an annual turnover of 160 million crowns would be taken over by the Haan-based German purchaser on January 1, 1997.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
</text>
